																		Re: The Safe, Dark Deep
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-hajovsky" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7041744); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7041744&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608474236" alt="Dr Hajovsky" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7041744)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dr-hajovsky" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(7041744); return false;" >Dr Hajovsky</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607960000 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">14 Dec 2020 15:33</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4844652">
									

<p>Overall, I'm a big fan of the way the article and story is presented. I like the way the logs record the slow degradation of the mental state of the team, and the eventual total breakdown of order. While it's nothing too original, it contains a pretty interesting narrative and SCP.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Some&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX holds two main anomalous properties.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This sentence and the use of &quot;Firstly&quot; and &quot;Secondly&quot; is a bit extraneous. I don't really see a need to state that their are two main anomalous properties when we are about to read them.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Hume readings in the area are incredibly low, indicating some force inside the cavern is altering reality. The side effects of this property make it so that conventional methods of terminating living organisms do not work (for reference please see Dr. Anna Lang’s research and SCP-3001).</p>
</blockquote>
<p>SCP-3001 is my personal favorite, so I'm glad to see it being referenced here. However, one of the major effects of low hume levels as presented in that article is that they cause the disintegration of physical matter over time. This isn't too much of a problem, since the cave's regenerative factors likely make up for this, but it might needed to be directly stated in the article if that's the case.</p>
<p>There are a pretty large amount of grammatical errors in the description and some in the logs. I just suggest giving these another once-over for errors.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Also, having read the Idea thread, I personally prefer &quot;The Abyss is Safe&quot; for the title. It sounds a bit more original and eye catching to me.</p>

							</div>

								
